.TH std::inplace_vector::empty 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::inplace_vector::empty \- std::inplace_vector::empty

.SH Synopsis
constexpr bool empty() const noexcept;  (since C++26)

Checks if the container has no elements, i.e. whether begin() == end().

.SH Parameters

\fI(none)\fP

.SH Return value

true if the container is empty, false otherwise.

.SH Complexity

Constant.

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <cassert>
#include <inplace_vector>

int main()
{
    std::inplace_vector<char, 8> v;
    assert(v.empty());

    v.push_back('_');
    assert(not v.empty());
}

.SH See also

size    returns the number of elements
        \fI(public member function)\fP
empty   checks whether the container is empty
\fI(C++17)\fP \fI(function template)\fP
